WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:16.699
looked at his permission slip.

2
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:21.581
The campers were going to Sunnydale Park today, but he didn't know why.

3
00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:23.382
Then Mr.

4
00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:24.742
Dunn solved the mystery.

5
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:28.244
"The Kite Festival is at the park today.

6
00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:31.234
And we're going to participate!"

7
00:00:31.254 --> 00:00:36.697
"But we don't have kites," said Jason.

8
00:00:36.717 --> 00:00:38.298
"Not yet.

9
00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:40.780
But we will soon," Mr.

10
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.460
Dunn said.

11
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.402
"Are we going shopping for kites?"

12
00:00:44.843 --> 00:00:45.663
Izzie asked.

13
00:00:46.724 --> 00:00:47.905
Mr. Dunn laughed.

14
00:00:50.346 --> 00:00:52.508
"We're going to make our kites, Izzie."

15
00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:56.230
Izzie cheered, but Nina frowned.

16
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.396
"That sounds hard," she said.

17
00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:02.218
"It's actually very easy."

18
00:01:03.198 --> 00:01:04.919
Mr. Dunn pointed to the table.

19
00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:11.462
"If we attach strings and tails to these paper bags, they should fly."

20
00:01:11.482 --> 00:01:14.364
"That sounds fun," said Ethan.

21
00:01:14.384 --> 00:01:16.045
"Let's get started."

22
00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:21.888
"First find the top of your bag, where it opens," said Mr.

23
00:01:21.928 --> 00:01:28.824
Dunn. "With masking tape, mark the four corners, two on each side.

24
00:01:29.985 --> 00:01:32.888
After that we'll punch a hole in each corner."

25
00:01:33.908 --> 00:01:35.330
The kids marked the corners.

26
00:01:37.712 --> 00:01:38.953
Then they punched the holes.

27
00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:46.499
we need to add string to fly our kites," said Mr.

28
00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:52.104
Dunn. "Cut two pieces of string 75 centimeters long.

29
00:01:55.344 --> 00:01:58.845
Thread one string through the left hole on one side of the bag.

30
00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:02.486
Tie a knot so the string won't slip through.

31
00:02:04.006 --> 00:02:09.428
Then thread the other end of the string through the right hole and knot it," said Mr.

32
00:02:09.468 --> 00:02:12.269
Dunn. "Repeat on the other side."

33
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:18.770
said Izzie.

34
00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.791
"I made two loops!"

35
00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:22.631
Next Mr.

36
00:02:22.671 --> 00:02:24.452
Dunn told them how to make the handles.

37
00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:28.493
"Cut a string 100 centimeters long.

38
00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:34.757
Pull it through the two loops you just made," Mr.

39
00:02:34.797 --> 00:02:35.697
Dunn continued.

40
00:02:35.717 --> 00:02:37.778
"And tie the ends."

41
00:02:39.279 --> 00:02:41.360
Mr. Dunn checked everyone's handles.

42
00:02:42.621 --> 00:02:46.243
"Fantastic! Now we're ready to decorate."

43
00:02:46.263 --> 00:02:50.785
"There will be lots of kites at the festival," said Mr.

44
00:02:50.825 --> 00:02:55.408
Dunn. "So paint your name in huge letters on your kite.

45
00:02:57.508 --> 00:03:02.290
After that, cut up some streamers and glue them to the bottom of your bag.

46
00:03:03.811 --> 00:03:04.571
Any questions?"

47
00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.312
Mr. Dunn looked around.

48
00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:10.814
"Nope." Ethan had already started painting.

49
00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:14.155
"I like those polka dots," said Izzie.

50
00:03:14.175 --> 00:03:16.296
"Very colorful!"

51
00:03:16.316 --> 00:03:21.858
"Thanks," said Ethan, adding orange and yellow streamers to the bottom of the bag.

52
00:03:21.878 --> 00:03:25.380
"I want my kite to look like a flaming comet!"

53
00:03:27.096 --> 00:03:29.739
After lunch it was finally time to go to the festival.

54
00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:34.323
"This looks really cool," Ethan said, admiring his kite.

55
00:03:35.403 --> 00:03:38.166
He tucked it under his arm and lined up behind Mr.

56
00:03:38.206 --> 00:03:43.010
Dunn. Ethan couldn't believe how crowded the park was.

57
00:03:44.151 --> 00:03:46.993
He didn't know there were so many kite-lovers in Sunnydale!

58
00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.637
Mr. Dunn pointed to an empty patch of grass.

59
00:03:50.657 --> 00:03:54.260
"We can launch our kites over there," he said.

60
00:03:58.268 --> 00:03:59.089
Ethan looked up.

61
00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:03.091
The sky was colorful as kites flew in every direction.

62
00:04:06.693 --> 00:04:08.193
worried," Jason said.

63
00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:10.595
"Maybe our kites won't fly."

64
00:04:10.615 --> 00:04:14.317
"You won't know until you try," Ethan said.

65
00:04:14.337 --> 00:04:15.817
"Come on!"

66
00:04:16.618 --> 00:04:19.139
He grabbed his kite's handle and started to run.

67
00:04:19.159 --> 00:04:21.781
"Yeah! Let's go!"

68
00:04:22.641 --> 00:04:25.002
Izzie grabbed her kite and ran after Ethan.

69
00:04:25.923 --> 00:04:27.884
Both of their kites took off in the wind.

70
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.663
Ethan weaved through the crowd with his kite soaring.

71
00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:36.169
Everyone's kites were different, but they all looked great.

72
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.192
Soon he saw Jason following him.

73
00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.975
Jason's kite was in the air too.

74
00:04:41.995 --> 00:04:44.398
"Doesn't it feel good to fly?"

75
00:04:44.759 --> 00:04:45.620
Ethan shouted.
